      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03144",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": " “苇手”是一种戏书，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Ashi-de is a kind of playful calligraphy,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03144",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "在色纸上用草书字母写歌，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "in which poems are written on colored paper in cursive characters,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03144",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "形似水边芦苇。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "with forms that resemble reeds by the water.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03144",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "“歌绘”是表现歌意的画，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Uta-e are pictures that express the meaning of poems,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03144",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "文字与画混合。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "mixing writing together with images.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03144",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "平安时代流行此二种书法。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "These two forms of calligraphy were popular in the Heian period.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
